ON DATA

Unlike the companion ML repository, this one downloads no datasets. All data
is SYNTHETIC, generated by 00_setup/make_data.py from a fixed seed, so no
third-party dataset licence applies to anything here. Nothing in this
repository is real data of any kind.

ON SOFTWARE FETCHED AT RUNTIME

Two examples rely on third-party tooling that is not part of this repository
and keeps its own licence:

  - 01_ingestion/02_kafka  EXPECTS an Apache Kafka release (Apache License
    2.0) already unpacked at ~/kafka. The script does not download it - it
    starts and stops a broker from what is there, and prints how to fetch the
    current release if the directory is missing.

  - 03_bigquery/02_dataform  fetches @dataform/cli via npx (Apache
    License 2.0). It is cached by npm, not vendored here.

The Google Cloud SDK emulators used by several examples (Pub/Sub, Bigtable,
Firestore) ship with the SDK and are governed by its terms. Those examples
DO invoke `gcloud` locally to start and stop an emulator; none of them calls
a Google Cloud API or needs a project.

ON PYTHON PACKAGES

Installed from requirements.txt by pip, not vendored here. Each keeps its
own licence:

  apache-beam            Apache License 2.0
  google-cloud-pubsub    Apache License 2.0
  confluent-kafka        Apache License 2.0
  pyarrow                Apache License 2.0
  numpy                  BSD 3-Clause
  matplotlib             Matplotlib licence (BSD-compatible)
  pyspark                Apache License 2.0
  redis                  MIT License
  google-cloud-bigtable  Apache License 2.0
  google-cloud-firestore Apache License 2.0

Apache Airflow (Apache License 2.0) is installed into its own virtualenv,
not from requirements.txt - see 05_orchestration/01_composer/README.md.

ON WHAT THE NUMBERS ARE WORTH

Runtimes, throughputs and costs quoted in the READMEs were MEASURED on one
laptop, and are stated as such. They will differ on yours. Nothing here is a
benchmark, and no figure in it is a substitute for Google's own pricing
calculator or documentation.
